<%- include("partials/header.ejs") %>

<a href="/" class="back-btn">
    <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Hub
</a>

<main class="container">
    <div class="post-container text-start">
        <div class="row align-items-center g-4">
            <div class="col-md-3 text-center">
                <div class="profile-circle mx-auto">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-people-group fa-4x"></i>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-9">
                <h1 class="display-5 mb-2">About Common Ground</h1>
                <p class="lead text-cyan mb-2">Community publishing with accountable moderation.</p>
                <p class="text-white-50 mb-0">
                    Common Ground is an Express + EJS platform where members create groups, publish posts,
                    comment, report harmful content, and manage moderation decisions with a full audit trail.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <hr class="my-5 border-secondary">

        <h2 class="h4 mb-3">What the platform includes</h2>
        <div class="row g-4 mb-2">
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <div class="about-card p-3 h-100">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-users text-cyan mb-2"></i>
                    <h5>Community foundations</h5>
                    <p class="small mb-0">Signup/login, user profiles, group creation, membership controls, and role-aware posting/commenting.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <div class="about-card p-3 h-100">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved text-cyan mb-2"></i>
                    <h5>Moderation queue</h5>
                    <p class="small mb-0">Report intake for posts/comments, open/resolved/dismissed workflows, single and bulk actions, and follow-up notes.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <div class="about-card p-3 h-100">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-filter text-cyan mb-2"></i>
                    <h5>Operational filtering</h5>
                    <p class="small mb-0">Queue search and filtering by status, reporter, and date range, with preserved state across moderation action tabs.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <div class="about-card p-3 h-100">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-chart-line text-cyan mb-2"></i>
                    <h5>Moderator insights</h5>
                    <p class="small mb-0">Community health signals, escalation watch, warning thresholds, 7-day trend summaries, and hot-spot leaderboards.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <div class="about-card p-3 h-100">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-clipboard-list text-cyan mb-2"></i>
                    <h5>Auditability</h5>
                    <p class="small mb-0">Every moderation decision is logged with actor, target, reason/follow-up note, and timestamp for accountability.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <div class="about-card p-3 h-100">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-server text-cyan mb-2"></i>
                    <h5>Deployment readiness</h5>
                    <p class="small mb-0">Database bootstrap on startup, session hardening, plus <code>/health</code> and <code>/ready</code> endpoints for liveness/readiness checks.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <hr class="my-5 border-secondary">

        <h2 class="h4 mb-3">Current direction</h2>
        <p class="text-white-50 mb-2">
            The project is in a stable hardening phase with end-to-end tests covering core auth,
            community flows, moderation controls, and dashboard-level moderation analytics.
        </p>
        <p class="text-white-50 mb-0">
            Next improvements focus on product polish and maintainability while preserving strict,
            test-backed delivery.
        </p>
    </div>
</main>

<%- include("partials/footer.ejs") %>